# Explainable AI Medical Diagnosis System — Project Rules

This is a university final-year project. Read this file fully before making
any changes. These rules apply to EVERY task, every conversation, without
needing to be repeated.

## PROTECTED FILES — NEVER MODIFY, REWRITE, OR "IMPROVE"

These are already built, tested, and verified working end-to-end:

- models/neural_network.py
- models/train.py
- models/lime_explainer.py
- models/risk_calculator.py
- server/database/queries.py
- server/auth.py
- server/otp_service.py
- server/server.py
- server/api_handler.py
- server/routes/\*.py

If a task seems to require changing one of these, STOP and ask first rather
than editing it.

## STRICT TECH STACK RULES

- AI Engine (models/): Pure Python + NumPy ONLY. No TensorFlow, scikit-learn,
  PyTorch, or any ML library. This is a hard academic requirement.
- Frontend: Pure HTML5 + CSS3 + Vanilla JavaScript ONLY. No React, Vue,
  Angular, TypeScript, Tailwind, or any build tool/framework. Chart.js via
  CDN is the only external library allowed.
- Backend: Python's built-in http.server module only. No Flask/Django/FastAPI.
- Database: MySQL via pymysql (already configured in
  server/database/db_connection.py — do not change its connection method).

## VERIFIED WORKING BACKEND — ACTUAL DETAILS (not the original spec's assumptions)

- Server runs on http://localhost:8081 (port 8080 is blocked by Windows on
  this machine, server auto-falls-back to 8081)
- Registration is 2-step OTP-based:
  1. POST /register/request-otp {name, email, password, role, institution}
  2. POST /register/verify-otp {email, otp}
- POST /login {email, password} -> {token, role, user_id, name}
- POST /logout — requires Authorization: Bearer <token>
- POST /forgot-password/request-otp {email}
- POST /forgot-password/reset {email, otp, new_password}
- POST /predict, GET /explain?id=X, POST /whatif, GET /history — ALL require
  header: Authorization: Bearer <token>
- GET /report?id=X currently returns 501 (not built yet)
- Error responses: {"success": false, "error": "message"} with proper HTTP
  status codes (400/401/404/500)

## DESIGN SYSTEM

Visual reference: https://pulse-diagnose.lovable.app (look only — do not
copy its React/TypeScript code, only the visual style and UX flow)

Colors (already in frontend/css/style.css):

- Background (navy): #0B1437
- Card background: #112257
- Primary accent (cyan): #00C2D4
- Secondary accent (purple): #7C3AED
- Success (green): #10B981 | Warning (amber): #F59E0B | Danger (red): #EF4444
- Font: Inter or Poppins (Google Fonts)
- Cards: 16px rounded corners, glassmorphism, glowing top border accent

## SESSION HANDLING

Store the session token in sessionStorage (not localStorage) — clears when
the browser tab closes, appropriate for a medical app. Attach it as an
Authorization: Bearer <token> header on every protected API call.

## GENERAL WORKING STYLE

- This is real, working software, not a toy demo — treat error handling,
  input validation, and correctness as required, not optional.
- Always test what you build yourself (using the browser tool or terminal)
  before saying a task is done. Report REAL results, not "should work."
- If anything is ambiguous or conflicts with what you find in the existing
  codebase, ask rather than guessing.
- Work in small stages when a task is large — build a few files, show me
  the result, then continue, rather than one giant unreviewed batch.
